package alkanes:dsigil;

/// DSIGIL — the capability that authorises `set-weightmap` on the FIREVECTOR VM.
///
/// Exactly one unit exists, minted at initialisation and never again. Authority
/// is possession: holding the unit and spending it into a call is the proof.
///
/// Note what is NOT here: there is no `authenticate` method.
///
/// The canonical auth-token pattern exposes one, and its implementation returns
/// two tokens where one went in — `CallResponse::forward(&incoming)` already sets
/// `alkanes = incoming`, then the same transfer is pushed again, and the runtime
/// permits an alkane to mint itself. Every authentication therefore inflates the
/// supply of the thing that is supposed to be unique. frSIGIL copies that pattern
/// byte for byte.
///
/// Omitting the method makes the bug unreachable rather than merely unused: there
/// is no callback to call, so "exactly one DSIGIL exists" is an invariant the
/// contract actually holds. The FIREVECTOR VM checks possession directly and
/// never calls back here.
interface dsigil {
    initialize: func() -> result<_, string>;
    get-name: func() -> result<string, string>;
    get-symbol: func() -> result<string, string>;
    get-total-supply: func() -> result<u64, string>;
}

world dsigil-world {
    export dsigil;
}
